@startuml 01-component
' =====================================================================
' Automated Code Feedback -- Component Architecture
' Traces to: NFR-3, NFR-4, NFR-11, FR-37, FR-38, FR-39
'
' Two structural facts that drive everything else:
'
'  1. The instructor's own test suite IS the autograder. We do not
'     invoke it. It imports our reporting library and calls us with the
'     target names the instructor registered in the web app. Control is
'     inverted relative to a framework: we ship a library, not a runner.
'
'  2. The AI grading component runs INSIDE the platform autograder
'     container, in both immediate and nightly mode. The nightly job
'     runner only triggers reruns; it never calls an LLM.
' =====================================================================

title Component Architecture

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam InterfaceBackgroundColor #FFFFFF

legend top right
  |= Colour |= Owner |= Stream |
  |<#D6E4F0>| Student A | AI grading and LLM orchestration |
  |<#DCEFD9>| Student B | Web app, DB schema, repository layer |
  |<#FBE6D4>| Student C | Reporting library, packager, nightly trigger |
  |<#EDE0F0>| Student D | Requirements, tests, CI/CD, docs |
  |<#FFF2CC>| Instructor | Written per course, NOT by us |
  |<#E8E8E8>| -- | External systems |
endlegend

actor Instructor as instr
actor Student as stud

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
' Our cloud service
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
package "Cloud-hosted Service (NFR-1)" {

  package "Instructor Web Application" #DCEFD9 {
    [Web Frontend] as fe #DCEFD9
    [Web Backend / REST API] as be #DCEFD9
  }

  package "Shared Data Layer" #DCEFD9 {
    [Repository Layer] as repo #DCEFD9
    database "Grading Database" as db #DCEFD9
  }
}

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
' Inside the LMS autograder container -- NOT our infrastructure
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
cloud "Gradescope (or other LMS)" as gs #E8E8E8 {

  [Submission UI] as gs_ui #E8E8E8
  [Feedback / Results View] as gs_fb #E8E8E8
  [Submission view\n(Rerun Autograder)] as gs_rerun #E8E8E8

  package "Autograder Container" as agbox #E8E8E8 {

    [Autograder Script\n(run_autograder)] as script #FFF2CC
    [Instructor Test Suite\n(JUnit / pytest / ...)] as tests_i #FFF2CC

    [Reporting Library\nJava jar + Python pkg] as wrapper #FBE6D4

    [AI Grading Phase] as aigrade #D6E4F0
    [results.json Packager] as packager #FBE6D4
  }
}

cloud "LLM Providers" as llms #E8E8E8 {
  [Anthropic API] as p_claude #E8E8E8
  [OpenAI API] as p_openai #E8E8E8
  [Google Gemini API] as p_gemini #E8E8E8
}

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
' Nightly trigger
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
package "Repository / CI-CD" #EDE0F0 {
  [Nightly Trigger Job\n(Playwright / Selenium)] as trigger #FBE6D4
  [Scheduled Workflow\n(cron)] as cron #EDE0F0
  [CI Workflow\n(on commit)] as ci #EDE0F0
  [Test Suite] as tests #EDE0F0
  [Instructor + Technical Docs] as docs #EDE0F0
}

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
' Published interfaces -- THE CONTRACTS
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
interface "IGradingRepository" as IRepo
interface "IReportingApi" as IReport
interface "ILearningPlatform" as IPlat
interface "ILLMProvider" as ILLM

repo -up- IRepo
be -up- IReport
trigger -up- IPlat
aigrade -up- ILLM

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
' Wiring
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
instr --> fe : registers targets, rubrics,\ngrading_mode
instr --> script : writes the autograder script\nand the test suite
fe --> be : HTTPS / JSON
be ..> IRepo
repo --> db : SQL

stud --> gs_ui : submits code
gs_ui --> script : container runs\nrun_autograder
script --> tests_i : 1. run the test suite
script --> aigrade : 2. invoke the AI phase

tests_i --> wrapper : ai_not_needed(target)\nadd_test_result(target, status,\nfunctional_test_feedback)
wrapper ..> IReport : HTTPS

aigrade --> packager
packager --> gs_fb : results.json
gs_fb --> stud : feedback

aigrade ..> IReport
aigrade ..> ILLM
p_claude <-- aigrade
p_openai <-- aigrade
p_gemini <-- aigrade

cron --> trigger : nightly
trigger --> gs_rerun : login, click "Rerun Autograder"\nper submission needing AI
gs_rerun --> agbox : re-runs the container

ci --> tests
tests ..> be
tests ..> aigrade
tests ..> wrapper
tests ..> trigger

note as N_OWN #FFF8DC
  **The instructor owns the two yellow boxes.**
  It is an ordinary JUnit or pytest suite. We do
  not generate it, invoke it, or constrain how
  it is structured. It imports the reporting
  library and calls us with the target names the
  instructor registered in the web app.

  The marking logic lives here too. Every
  registered target wants feedback by default,
  and she opts targets out by calling
  ai_not_needed: on passing tests, on a subset,
  on any condition she can express in code.

  She can also report the outcome via
  add_test_result: status for the dashboard, and
  an optional functional_test_feedback string
  carried into the prompt.

  run_autograder is hers as well: it decides to
  run her suite and then invoke our AI phase.
end note

note as N_WRAP #FFF8DC
  Thin by design: two calls, an HTTPS client,
  and argument validation. One artifact per
  language the courses use.

  It rejects an unregistered target name loudly
  on the first call, failing her test run. A
  typo that silently succeeds is the worst
  failure mode here: everything looks like it
  worked and the feedback simply never appears.
end note

note as N_AIP #FFF8DC
  Invoked by the instructor's autograder script
  as a separate command after her suite exits,
  not from inside her test code.

  Invoked by the instructor's script in EVERY
  run, including the submission run of a NIGHTLY
  assignment. It asks the service for one action
  and performs it: GRADE, DEFER or REEMIT.

  It holds no policy. Grading mode, the nightly
  authorisation flag and the token guard are all
  derived server-side, because this code ships
  inside the instructor's autograder zip and is
  the hardest thing in the system to update.
end note

note as N_TRIG #FFF8DC
  Log in, then click Rerun Autograder once per
  submission that still has tasks marked
  ai_needed. It does NOT call an LLM and does
  NOT write feedback.
end note

note as N_KEYS #FFF8DC
  **AD-4: the container holds the instructor's
  own LLM API key** and calls the providers
  directly. Our service never proxies an LLM
  call and never sees a provider key.

  For an OER this is the right default: each
  adopting institution uses its own key and pays
  its own bill, so nobody has to run a metered
  service or handle someone else's billing.

  The container still holds NO database
  credential. It reaches our data only through
  IReportingApi with a per-assignment token.

  Two things to settle in the instructor guide,
  not in code. How the key gets into the
  container, which depends on what secret
  facility the platform offers; if the only
  route is the uploaded autograder zip, say so
  plainly, because a key in a zip is a key in a
  backup. And that rotation means touching every
  assignment that carries it.
end note

@enduml
